#: ../../library/imu.rst:2
msgid ":mod:`imu` --- IMU helper for the Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense"
msgstr ":mod:`imu` --- asistente de IMU para la Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense"

#: ../../library/imu.rst:10
msgid ""
"This page documents the Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense's Python ``imu`` module (a"
" small wrapper around the on-board IMU drivers). For the OpenMV C-level "
"``imu`` module that ships on the OPENMV_N6, OPENMV_RT1060, and OPENMV_AE3 "
"camera boards, see :doc:`omv.imu`."
msgstr ""
"Esta página documenta el módulo ``imu`` de Python de la Arduino Nano 33 BLE "
"Sense (un pequeño contenedor alrededor de los controladores de IMU "
"integrados). Para el módulo ``imu`` a nivel de C de OpenMV que se incluye en"
" las placas de cámara OPENMV_N6, OPENMV_RT1060 y OPENMV_AE3, consulte "
":doc:`omv.imu`."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:15
msgid ""
"This module is a thin board-specific wrapper that exposes the on-board "
"inertial measurement unit of the Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense as a single "
":py:class:`~imu.IMU` object. Both hardware revisions of the board are "
"handled transparently:"
msgstr ""
"Este módulo es un contenedor ligero específico de la placa que expone la "
"unidad de medición inercial integrada de la Arduino Nano 33 BLE Sense como "
"un único objeto :py:class:`~imu.IMU`. Ambas revisiones de hardware de la "
"placa se gestionan de forma transparente:"

#: ../../library/imu.rst:20
msgid "**Rev 1** uses a single LSM9DS1 9-axis IMU."
msgstr "La **Rev 1** utiliza una única IMU LSM9DS1 de 9 ejes."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:21
msgid ""
"**Rev 2** combines a Bosch BMI270 (accelerometer + gyroscope) with a Bosch "
"BMM150 magnetometer."
msgstr ""
"La **Rev 2** combina un Bosch BMI270 (acelerómetro + giroscopio) con un "
"magnetómetro Bosch BMM150."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:24
msgid ""
"The constructor probes the I2C bus for the BMI270 address (``0x68``) and "
"selects the matching driver automatically, so user code can be written once "
"and run on either revision."
msgstr ""
"El constructor sondea el bus I2C en busca de la dirección del BMI270 "
"(``0x68``) y selecciona automáticamente el controlador correspondiente, de "
"modo que el código de usuario se puede escribir una sola vez y ejecutar en "
"cualquiera de las dos revisiones."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:28
msgid "Example::"
msgstr "Ejemplo::"

#: ../../library/imu.rst:45
msgid "class IMU"
msgstr "class IMU"

#: ../../library/imu.rst:49
msgid "Construct an IMU object bound to an I2C bus."
msgstr "Construye un objeto IMU vinculado a un bus I2C."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:51
msgid ""
"*bus* is an initialised :py:class:`machine.I2C` instance connected to the "
"on-board IMU(s)."
msgstr ""
"*bus* es una instancia inicializada de :py:class:`machine.I2C` conectada a "
"la(s) IMU integrada(s)."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:54
msgid ""
"On construction the bus is scanned: if a device responds at address ``0x68``"
" a `BMI270` plus `BMM150` pair is instantiated (Nano 33 BLE Sense Rev 2), "
"otherwise an `LSM9DS1` is instantiated (Rev 1). The underlying driver is "
"kept on the ``imu`` attribute and configured with default ranges and output "
"data rates."
msgstr ""
"Durante la construcción se escanea el bus: si un dispositivo responde en la "
"dirección ``0x68`` se instancia un par `BMI270` más `BMM150` (Nano 33 BLE "
"Sense Rev 2), de lo contrario se instancia un `LSM9DS1` (Rev 1). El "
"controlador subyacente se mantiene en el atributo ``imu`` y se configura con"
" rangos y tasas de datos de salida predeterminados."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:62
msgid ""
"Return the latest accelerometer reading as an ``(x, y, z)`` tuple in units "
"of *g* (standard gravities)."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve la última lectura del acelerómetro como una tupla ``(x, y, z)`` en "
"unidades de *g* (gravedades estándar)."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:67
msgid ""
"Return the latest gyroscope reading as an ``(x, y, z)`` tuple in degrees per"
" second."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve la última lectura del giroscopio como una tupla ``(x, y, z)`` en "
"grados por segundo."

#: ../../library/imu.rst:72
msgid ""
"Return the latest magnetometer reading as an ``(x, y, z)`` tuple in micro-"
"tesla (uT)."
msgstr ""
"Devuelve la última lectura del magnetómetro como una tupla ``(x, y, z)`` en "
"microteslas (uT)."
